220,21,1124,408,90,5187,2555,31716,323,57960,10374,13233,90,66,92,284,1124,7265,90,5187,2555,92,220,17,24984,481,22,24984,481,16,15,1124,408,90,5187,2555,92,2418,220,7379,279,7192,897,315,198,59,26056,10374,13233,90,66,92,1124,50853,19788,10374,13233,90,64,92,1124,15136,1124,10374,13233,90,65,38842,59,60,2870,57960,10374,13233,90,64,31716,374,264,4982,4621,13,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nLet $\\mathbf{b} = \\begin{pmatrix} -1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 6 \\end{pmatrix}$ and $\\mathbf{c} = \\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\\\ -7 \\\\ -10 \\end{pmatrix}.$  Find the maximum value of\n\\[\\mathbf{c} \\cdot (\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b}),\\]where $\\mathbf{a}$ is a unit vector.","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"19d818f8ecdfc25e423979565165654df309e6994d6190fc58c5abe6c8e7304c"},"seconds":54.229188203811646,"seed":79307383336384083,"stop":"eos","text":"To find the maximum value of $\\mathbf{c} \\cdot (\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b})$, where $\\mathbf{a}$ is a unit vector, we will use the properties of the dot and cross products.\n\nFirst, let's write down the vectors given in the problem:\n\\[\n\\mathbf{b} = \\begin{pmatrix} -1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 6 \\end{pmatrix}, \\quad \\mathbf{c} = \\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\\\ -7 \\\\ -10 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nThe expression $\\mathbf{c} \\cdot (\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b})$ is a scalar triple product. The scalar triple product $\\mathbf{c} \\cdot (\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b})$ can be interpreted geometrically as the volume of the parallelepiped formed by the vectors $\\mathbf{a}$, $\\mathbf{b}$, and $\\mathbf{c}$.\n\nThe magnitude of the scalar triple product is maximized when $\\mathbf{a}$ is chosen such that $\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b}$ is parallel to $\\mathbf{c}$. This occurs when $\\mathbf{a}$ is chosen to maximize the projection of $\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b}$ onto $\\mathbf{c}$.\n\nThe magnitude of $\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b}$ is given by:\n\\[\n|\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b}| = |\\mathbf{a}| |\\mathbf{b}| \\sin\\theta\n\\]\nSince $\\mathbf{a}$ is a unit vector, $|\\mathbf{a}| = 1$, so:\n\\[\n|\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b}| = |\\mathbf{b}| \\sin\\theta\n\\]\nThe maximum value of $\\sin\\theta$ is 1, so:\n\\[\n|\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b}| = |\\mathbf{b}|\n\\]\n\nNext, we need to find the magnitude of $\\mathbf{b}$:\n\\[\n|\\mathbf{b}| = \\sqrt{(-1)^2 + 4^2 + 6^2} = \\sqrt{1 + 16 + 36} = \\sqrt{53}\n\\]\n\nThe maximum value of $\\mathbf{c} \\cdot (\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b})$ is then:\n\\[\n|\\mathbf{c}| |\\mathbf{b}| \\cos\\phi\n\\]\nwhere $\\phi$ is the angle between $\\mathbf{c}$ and $\\mathbf{b} \\times \\mathbf{a}$. Since we want to maximize this value, $\\cos\\phi$ should be maximized, which is 1 when $\\mathbf{c}$ is parallel to $\\mathbf{b} \\times \\mathbf{a}$.\n\nNow, we calculate the magnitude of $\\mathbf{c}$:\n\\[\n|\\mathbf{c}| = \\sqrt{2^2 + (-7)^2 + (-10)^2} = \\sqrt{4 + 49 + 100} = \\sqrt{153}\n\\]\n\nThus, the maximum value of $\\mathbf{c} \\cdot (\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b})$ is:\n\\[\n|\\mathbf{c}| |\\mathbf{b}| = \\sqrt{153} \\cdot \\sqrt{53} = \\sqrt{153 \\cdot 53}\n\\]\n\nCalculating the product inside the square root:\n\\[\n153 \\cdot 53 = 8109\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the maximum value is:\n\\[\n\\sqrt{8109}\n\\]\n\nSo, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\sqrt{8109}}\n\\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{\\sqrt{8109}}","correct":false,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
